		<title type="html"><![CDATA[TYT MD-2017 / RT-82 • Re: MD-2017 running latest OpenMDUV380(openGD77)]]></title>

					<category term="TYT MD-2017 / RT-82" scheme="http://localhost/opengd77/viewforum.php?f=26" label="TYT MD-2017 / RT-82"/>
		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2714&amp;p=24888#p24888"><![CDATA[
The Retevis RT-82 is their clone of the TYT MD-2017. The radios can use each other's firmware and CPS. It's not surprising that it would misbehave in the same way with existing firmware.<br><br>The most difficult part of supporting any of these might be the mini-trackball. Then again, it's the worst feature of the radio and it has plenty of buttons, so it wouldn't be horrible if the trackball isn't implemented at all.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4032">KE1L</a> — Tue Aug 08, 2023 3:12 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
